===============================================================================

Rails Onboarding has been installed!

Next steps:

1. Run the migration:
   rails db:migrate

2. Add the Onboardable concern to your User model:

   # app/models/user.rb
   class User < ApplicationRecord
     include RailsOnboarding::Onboardable

     # your existing code...
   end

3. Configure onboarding in config/initializers/rails_onboarding.rb

4. Set up JavaScript controllers (see ESBUILD_SETUP.md for details):
   - Copy JavaScript files to app/javascript/controllers/rails_onboarding/
   - Register controllers in app/javascript/controllers/index.js

5. Include CSS in your application:
   Add to app/assets/stylesheets/application.css:
   /*
    *= require rails_onboarding/application
    */

6. Add onboarding check to your ApplicationController (optional):

   class ApplicationController < ActionController::Base
     # Enable automatic onboarding redirect
     enable_onboarding_check except: [:show, :edit] # customize as needed
   end

7. Visit /onboarding to test your setup!

For more details, check the Rails Onboarding documentation.

===============================================================================
